---
description: Defines code quality standards for the entire 7Oz Espresso Cafe platform.
alwaysApply: true
---

# Code Quality

Every piece of code must be written for long-term maintainability.

Optimize for readability first.

Never optimize for fewer lines of code.

---

# Engineering Principles

Always follow:

- SOLID
- DRY
- KISS
- YAGNI
- Separation of Concerns
- Composition over Inheritance
- Feature-based Architecture

---

# Clean Code

Write code that is:

- Readable
- Predictable
- Consistent
- Self-documenting

Avoid clever code.

Prefer obvious code.

---

# Duplication

Never duplicate:

- Components
- Business Logic
- API Calls
- Validation Logic
- Utility Functions
- Constants
- Types

Always reuse existing code.

---

# Functions

Functions should:

Do one thing.

Return one responsibility.

Avoid deep nesting.

Prefer early return.

Target:

Maximum 40 lines when practical.

---

# Files

Keep files focused.

Avoid files exceeding approximately 300 lines unless justified.

Split by responsibility.

---

# Magic Values

Never hardcode:

- Colors
- URLs
- API Paths
- Roles
- Statuses
- Timeouts
- Limits

Use constants or configuration.

---

# Comments

Avoid explaining what the code does.

Explain WHY when necessary.

Good code should explain itself.

---

# Naming

Names should describe intention.

Bad

process()

Good

calculateLoyaltyPoints()

---

# Error Handling

Never ignore errors.

Never swallow exceptions.

Always handle expected failures.

---

# Logging

Log useful information.

Never log sensitive information.

---

# Refactoring

Leave the code cleaner than you found it.

---

# Technical Debt

Never knowingly introduce technical debt.

If unavoidable,

document it.

---

# Definition of Clean Code

Easy to read.

Easy to modify.

Easy to test.

Easy to review.

Easy to remove.